SOAPBOX: I intended to participate to this one on a reduced effort,
SOAPBOX: but once balls were rolling I could not stop. At the end I
SOAPBOX: increased my best score from last year by ~6%, not a big
SOAPBOX: number but considering I also had longer breaks, I am very satisfied.
SOAPBOX: 20m were death at the contest start, so I spent the first 2
SOAPBOX: hours running on 40/80, then the rest of the competition has
SOAPBOX: been all the time trade-off between run and mult catching,
SOAPBOX: excepts some focused run during the NA openings.
SOAPBOX: On Saturday, there were not much of US west coast stations
SOAPBOX: on 10-15 and a lot of signals from central/north US were
SOAPBOX: affected by aurora distortion. On Sunday the conditions on
SOAPBOX: the high bands improved a lot. Anyways 10-15 closed quite
SOAPBOX: early after the sunset, and also 20m didn't go for long time.
SOAPBOX: In general signals strength on high bands was average on even lower.
SOAPBOX: On the lower bands, the noise was really low and signals were
SOAPBOX: very clear, on 80, I worked easily ZL7 after my sunrise on Sunday.
SOAPBOX: On 40m, there was a very good opening with big signals with
SOAPBOX: JA/BY/YB and other far east on Sunday ~2 hours before the end.
SOAPBOX: Overall a very enjoyable weekend!
SOAPBOX: Congratulations to Dan, the new record will last many years
SOAPBOX: if not for ever, kudos to Chris as well, for his effort from
SOAPBOX: Madeira.
SOAPBOX: Thanks everyone to call-in,
SOAPBOX: 73's Luca IK2PFL
